      "description": "Watch Samsunspor vs Yeni Çorumspor highlights and goals from Süper Lig on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 12, 2026. The Süper Lig encounter on September 12, 2026 , delivered a high-octane performance that left fans breathless from the opening whistle. As Samsunspor and Besiktas faced off, the tactical battle on the pitch evolved into a clinical scoring spectacle. A Whirlwind Opening The match began with an intensity rarely seen, as Jesus Ramirez found the back of the net in the very first minute, setting a frantic pace for the evening. Before the visitors could even catch their breath, the advantage was doubled in the 5th minute when Logi Tomasson converted a chance created by Emre Kilinc . The onslaught continued as Cengiz Under took center stage, scoring twice in quick succession. His first goal arrived in the 10th minute following a Fredy assist, and he struck again in the 15th minute after being played through by Mohamed Diomande , leaving the opposition stunned by a four-goal blitz in the opening quarter-hour. Tactical Adjustments and Substitutions As the first half progressed, the tempo eventually settled, though the physical nature of the game increased, evidenced by a yellow card for Gokhan Sazdagi in the 31st minute. Following the halftime break, both managers looked to their benches to influence the flow. Berat Ozdemir replaced Mohamed Diomande early in the second period, while a flurry of changes around the hour mark saw the introduction of Youssoufa Moukoko and Ermin Mahmic . These tactical shifts provided fresh energy as the contest entered its final stages, ensuring the intensity remained high despite the early lead. Closing the Chapter The drama was far from over in the second half. In the 69th minute, Alexandros Kyziridis produced a clinical finish assisted by the newly introduced Ermin Mahmic . However, the response was immediate; just two minutes later, Jesus Ramirez secured his brace in the 71st minute after excellent work from Gokhan Sazdagi . Despite late bookings for Ylber Ramadani and Andrei Borza , and further substitutions including Haluk Mustafa Tan and Alexandre Penetra , the scoreline remained unchanged until the final whistle at 90+3 minutes, concluding a breathless Süper Lig fixture."
